{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9xTDUbiSXtvPYihAtdX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed when `Hijack()` refuses to take over the connection. Before, it failed as soon as anything had been sent, including just the headers. That broke websocket libraries like `github.com/coder/websocket`, which send headers first and then hijack.\n\n- **Fix (`response_writer.go`):** `Hijack()` now returns the error only once body bytes have been written. If only the headers have gone out, for example after `WriteHeaderNow()` or `Flush()`, it goes ahead. I also reworded the error to `gin: response body already written`.\n- **Test (`response_writer_test.go`):** I added a case where headers are written and then the hijack succeeds. The existing case where the body is written first and the hijack fails still passes.\n\nAll tests pass and `gofmt` reports nothing. I haven't committed; say if you want it committed under your subject line.\n\n**Risk:** a hijack after headers-only is now allowed. If the wrapped writer has already flushed those headers to the client, the hijacking code has to know that."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":164,"cache_read_input_tokens":36274,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":164,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83d0ab1c-dcf3-4295-b557-2be51bf2ecb8","uuid":"75d89742-02f1-451e-8f8e-1dfbe12733a2","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:41:53.570Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9xTDHBtY4NWADEZJkDa"}
